  "query_preview": "..\n(Tomorrow through Saturday)\nIssued at 1256 PM CDT Sat Sep 12 2026\n\nShowers and storms may linger into Sunday morning across far\nnorthwest Arkansas before ending. A strong upper ridge will then\nbuild over the area and persist through at least the middle of\nnext week with the center of the ridge just to our east. Dangerous\nheat will return Sunday through at least the middle of next week,\nwith daily heat headlines expected. A heat advisory has been\nissued for Sunday afternoon for much of eastern Oklahoma and west\ncentral Arkansas.\n\nShower and thunderstorm chances may increase by late week as a\ncold front approaches from the north. The timing of this front\nremains somewhat uncertain, but it does appear that a more\nsignificant cooldown may take place by sometime next weekend.",
